{=============================================================================
  Air handling unit with moist-air conditioning
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0028
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Supply air for a room comes from outdoors (30 °C, 60 % relative humidity).
  The supply conditions are achieved with an air handling unit: a cooling coil
  characterised by its contact effectiveness (80 %) followed by post-heating.
  The model computes the supply air state from the room sensible and moisture
  loads, the cooling coil capacity, the post-heating power and the condensate
  flow rate at the cooling coil. Original problem statement in French, exercise
  VL050429 (repetition 10, exercise 3).

  The native file keeps the EES syntax and does not run in CoolSolve: the
  contact temperature T_c is evaluated with
  T_c = temperature(AirH2O, P=P_in, w=w_c, R=1) (gap CS-GAP-PSYCHRO-SAT).
  The runnable transcription air_handling_unit_moist_air_coolsolve.eescode
  evaluates the same temperature with dewpoint() and reproduces the stored
  solution of the original EES file. See README.md.

  Inputs : P_in, T_in, RH_in, M_dot_w, V_dot_a, Q_dot_t, T_out, RH_out,
           epsilon_c
  Outputs: T_su, w_su, RH_su, M_dot_a, T_c, T_ex_bat, Q_dot_pc, M_dot_w_cond,
           Q_dot_batt, T[i], w[i]
  Units  : SI - temperatures in °C, pressures in Pa, energies in J
  Source : ULiège exercise (VL050429, repetition 10, exercise 3), rewritten as
           CoolSolve example humidair2 by S. Quoilin - see README.md
=============================================================================}

"VL050429
Repetition 10, exercise 3

The air supplied to the room of the previous exercise comes from outdoors.
The outdoor air temperature is 30 °C and its relative humidity is 60 %. The
supply conditions are achieved with an air handling unit. Calculate the heat
exchanged at the cooling coil (contact effectiveness of 80 %), the power
needed for post-heating and the condensate flow rate at the cooling coil.
"

P_in=1E5 "outdoor and room air pressure [Pa]"
T_in=25 "room air temperature [C]"
RH_in=0.5 "room air relative humidity [-]"
M_dot_w=0.08/3600 "[kg/s]"
V_dot_a=40/3600 "[m^3/s]"
Q_dot_t=130 "[W]"

"supply air conditions"
Q_dot_t=M_dot_a*(h_in-h_su) "room sensible energy balance [W]"
h_in=ENTHALPY(AirH2O,T=T_in,P=P_in,R=RH_in) "room air specific enthalpy [J/kg dry air]"
M_dot_a=V_dot_a/v_a_su "dry-air mass flow rate [kg/s dry air]"

v_a_su=volume(airH2O,T=T_su{in},P=P_in,w=w_su{in}) "supply air specific volume [m^3/kg dry air], for updating initial guesses"
T_su=temperature(airH2O,h=h_su,P=P_in,w=w_su) "supply air temperature [C]"

"water mass balance"
M_dot_a*w_su+M_dot_w=M_dot_a*w_in "room moisture balance [kg/s]"
w_in=humrat(airH2O,T=T_in,P=P_in,R=RH_in) "room air humidity ratio [kg/kg dry air]"

RH_su=Relhum(AIRH2O,P=P_in,T=T_su,w=w_su) "supply air relative humidity [-]"

"outdoor conditions"

T_out=30 "outdoor air temperature [C]"
RH_out=0.60 "outdoor air relative humidity [-]"
	"cooling coil"
epsilon_c=0.8 "coil contact effectiveness [-]"
epsilon_c=(w_out-w_su)/(w_out-w_c) "to compute w_c [-]"
w_out=humrat(airH2O,T=T_out,R=RH_out,P=P_in) "outdoor air humidity ratio [kg/kg dry air]"
T_c=temperature(airH2O,P=P_in,w=w_c,R=1) "coil contact temperature [C]"
epsilon_c=(T_out-T_ex_bat)/(T_out-T_c) "contact effectiveness on the temperatures [-]"

	"post-heating"
Q_dot_pc=M_dot_a*(h_su-h_ex_bat) "post-heating power [W]"
h_ex_bat=enthalpy(airH2O,P=P_in,T=T_ex_bat,w=w_su) "air enthalpy at the coil outlet [J/kg dry air]"
 "or"
Q_dot_pc_bis=M_dot_a*(h_su_air-h_ex_bat_air) "same power from the dry-air enthalpies only [W], as in the original"
h_su_air=enthalpy(air,T=T_su) "supply dry-air specific enthalpy [J/kg]"
h_ex_bat_air=enthalpy(air,T=T_ex_bat) "coil-outlet dry-air specific enthalpy [J/kg]"

	"condensate flow rate"
M_dot_w_cond=M_dot_a*(w_out-w_su) "water condensed at the cooling coil [kg/s]"

	"cooling coil capacity"
h_out=enthalpy(airH2O,P=P_in,T=T_out,w=w_out) "outdoor air specific enthalpy [J/kg dry air]"
Q_dot_batt=M_dot_a*(h_out-h_ex_bat) "cooling coil capacity [W]"

 	"Q_dot_pc equals Q_dot_pc_bis since there is no latent heat exchange after the cooling coil (humidity ratio stays at w_su)"

"states for the psychrometric chart"
T[1]=T_out "outdoor state [C]"
w[1]=w_out "outdoor humidity ratio [kg/kg dry air]"
T[2]=T_ex_bat "coil outlet state [C]"
w[2]=w_su "coil outlet humidity ratio [kg/kg dry air]"
T[3]=T_su "supply state [C]"
w[3]=w_su "supply humidity ratio [kg/kg dry air]"
T[4]=T_in "room state [C]"
w[4]=w_in "room humidity ratio [kg/kg dry air]"
